<BaseLayout title="About — Poor Louis Labs"><div class="shell"><section class="hero"><div><div class="eyebrow">About the practice</div><h1>Independent work, public evidence.</h1><p class="lede">Poor Louis Labs is an independent Alaskan research and engineering practice led by Alexander Collamore, with work spanning open standards, coding-agent infrastructure, experimental computing, construction tools, creative software, and the technical systems supporting Poor Louis Farms.</p></div></section><section class="section prose"><h2>What the name covers</h2><p>Poor Louis Labs is not a university, accredited laboratory, standards body, or large company. It is a public home for connected projects developed through practical engineering, open documentation, machine-assisted implementation, and explicit technical review.</p><h2>Relationship to Poor Louis Farms</h2><p>Poor Louis Farms is the family farm and commercial operation creating teas, spices, hot sauces, body products, flowers, and other Alaskan goods. Poor Louis Labs is the research, software, technical, and experimental companion. The Square storefront remains the source of truth for commerce.</p><h2>Publication standard</h2><p>Projects are described according to their public documentation. Prototypes are not presented as products, exploratory results are not presented as conclusions, and assurance claims remain scoped to the evidence and policy that support them.</p></section></div></BaseLayout>
